# Security headers for the static-asset Worker (frontend/wrangler.jsonc).
#
# Vite copies public/ into dist/, and Workers static assets read _headers from the served
# directory — so this file ships as-is with `npm run deploy`. Rules match top-down; `/*`
# covers every route because the app is a SPA served from one asset bundle.
#
# Every allowance below was derived from what the code actually loads, not from a template.
# If you add a new external origin, a directive here has to grow with it or the browser
# blocks it silently apart from a console message.
#
#   storage.cardcarp.com — card art (img), the two homepage hero .webm files (media),
#                          @font-face in main.css (font), SVG cursors, and set/card JSON
#                          fetched at runtime (connect). A <video> is NOT covered by
#                          img-src; it needs media-src or it falls back to default-src.
#   *.workers.dev        — the multiplayer relay (VITE_MULTIPLAYER_WS_URL). Tighten to the
#                          exact relay origin once it has a stable hostname; the wildcard is
#                          here only because the subdomain is account-specific. If the relay
#                          moves to a custom domain, this line must change or multiplayer
#                          stops connecting.
#   data: / blob:        — the jsPDF/JSZip print+export path, and Pixi's own asset worker,
#                          which it builds from a Blob URL (worker-src) to decode textures
#                          off the main thread. That worker inherits this policy, so its
#                          fetches to storage.cardcarp.com are covered by connect-src above.
#
#                          data: appears in connect-src for one reason, and it is not ours:
#                          before Pixi will use that worker it feature-tests createImageBitmap
#                          by fetch()ing a 1x1 white PNG as a data URL. fetch() of a data: URL
#                          is governed by connect-src, so without it the probe throws, Pixi
#                          reads the throw as "ImageBitmap unsupported", and every texture
#                          decodes on the main thread instead. It fails quietly — the art still
#                          appears — so the only symptoms are a violation report and a slower
#                          table. Widening connect-src by a whole scheme normally deserves a
#                          hard look; data: is the exception, because a data: URL is self-
#                          contained and has no server at the other end. There is nowhere for
#                          it to send anything, which is the thing connect-src exists to stop.
#
# Deliberately NOT locked down:
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline' — 43 components render literal style="..." attributes, and
#                          reka-ui/motion-v inject style tags at runtime. Removing it breaks
#                          dialogs, animations, and card layout. script-src stays strict,
#                          which is where the real XSS protection lives.
#   Permissions-Policy has no clipboard entry — navigator.clipboard.writeText backs the
#                          "copy room code" button and the deck export dialog.
#
# Deliberately kept strict, against pressure:
#   script-src has no 'unsafe-eval' — Pixi compiles its uniform-sync and shader-sync routines
#                          with `new Function` and refuses to start a renderer without it. The
#                          answer is Pixi's own `pixi.js/unsafe-eval` polyfill, imported in
#                          canvas-pixi/scene.js, NOT a directive here. If the table ever throws
#                          "Current environment does not allow unsafe-eval" again, that import
#                          is what went missing; adding the keyword back would trade the app's
#                          main XSS defence for microseconds in a scene that is batcher-bound.
#
# Deliberately locked to 'none' (verified unused, so these cost nothing and shut down a
# whole class of injected-markup attacks):
#   script-src-attr — no inline on*= handlers anywhere; Vue binds via addEventListener.
#   form-action     — the app contains no <form> at all.
#   frame-src       — no iframes; the YouTube/Proton links are plain anchors, and CSP does
#                     not restrict navigation, only embedding.
#   manifest-src    — no web app manifest is linked from index.html.
#   base-uri        — no <base> element; blocking it stops injected markup from repointing
#                     every relative URL on the page.
#
# HSTS is scoped to this host only — no includeSubDomains, no preload. storage/git/chat are
# separate subdomains, and committing them to HTTPS-forever from here would be a decision
# made in the wrong place. Preload especially is close to irreversible; do that at the zone
# level, deliberately, if you ever want it.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://storage.cardcarp.com; media-src 'self' https://storage.cardcarp.com; font-src 'self' https://storage.cardcarp.com; connect-src 'self' data: https://storage.cardcarp.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(self), bluetooth=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), local-fonts=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), serial=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
